      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "People say, vote with your wallet.\n\nPeople who do not like an aspect of something will avoid it. Some do and want it. That's their choice.\n\nIn this case, people will vote with their visits. If they don't like something, they don't want to see it. Just like seeing the same ad on TV/Youtube over and over again, you're less interested in the product/concept each time.\n\nIf your world/avatar is created with that aspect, those people will avoid you, and others who do, will enjoy. It's as simple as that.\n\nBut, in the event the masses prefer to not accept an aspect, and prefer to avoid it, they will, and the creator will have less foot traffic.\n\nSome creators are going through means to hide these aspects to get people to join, yet people will leave as soon as they join. Wasting people's times, further annoying them, more complaints come up, and less people willing to world hop due to additional wasted effort.\n\nI've been in small groups of world hoppers, AI worlds tend to get maybe 5-10minutes of time before someone drops down another portal and everyone forgets.\n\nGood Creators are honest with what they use for their worlds. Listing AI should be part of that. And I applaud those point out where they used AI. I know of at least one (it's my home world, and the AI use case isn't effecting the world directly, but for an information panel).\n\nPersonally, I'd be more willing, not so much the same level as a non-ai touched, to visit the world if the creator is honest and up front.\n\nAI has been over used in places where a human, a skilled human, should have done it. As someone who works in IT, I see thousands of others in IT and media creation losing their jobs, because someone wanted to save a few dollars, at the cost of quality. Ford is rehiring staff because of how AI has damaged their quality and wasted so much time and money.\n\nThis filter helps reduce these nuance headaches. Just like \"Hide This Avatar Globally\" would, hiding that Avatar ID no matter who wore the avatar.\n\nJust like using a websearch, we can add a - before a word, to force-exclude those listings, say I want pictures of animals, but exclude elephants. \"Animals -elephants\". As we currently sit, we cannot tag/classify something as AI-Used to begin filtering it out.\n\nRefusing to flag a world as created \"with AI\", speaking over all, should be seen as on par with not flagging a world Jump Scare/Gore or Adult Content.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
